Short:        rsync client (protocol 32, delta transfer)
Author:       Paul Hill
Uploader:     Paul Hill
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1
Requires:     68020+, bsdsocket.library (Roadshow, AmiTCP, Miami)

arsync copies files from and to rsync daemons (rsync 3.0 or newer) using
rsync's own protocol, version 32, including delta transfer: a big file with
small changes is updated by sending only the changes, in either direction.

  arsync rsync://host/                      list modules
  arsync rsync://host/module/dir            list files
  arsync -rtv rsync://host/module/dir Work:Dir
  arsync -t host::module/file RAM:file
  arsync -rtv Work:Projects/ rsync://host/module/backup

Features
  - pull and push, recursive (-r), modification times (-t), dry run (-n),
    progress (-P), verbose output and transfer summary (-v), --stats
  - delta transfer (MD5 block checksums), or whole files with -W
  - compression (-z, zlib and zlibx); packed files (.lha, .lzx, .dms,
    .zip...) are sent as they are
  - --exclude, --include, --exclude-from, --include-from, --filter,
    with rsync's pattern rules
  - --delete and --delete-excluded, in both directions
  - password-protected modules (--password-file, RSYNC_PASSWORD, or prompt)
  - output, options and exit codes like rsync's, so scripts carry over
  - files AmigaDOS can't hold (':' in names, names too long for the
    volume, names differing only in case, files of 2 GB or more) are
    skipped with a warning, never renamed
  - times converted to local time with the Locale time zone
  - Ctrl-C works at any point and leaves no half-written files
  - runs on its own 64 KB stack, so the Shell stack size doesn't matter

Not supported: symlinks, permissions, ssh.

Installation: copy arsync to C: (or anywhere in your path).

Source and documentation: see README.md in the source distribution.
Licence: MIT. Written from scratch; contains no rsync code. Includes
zlib 1.3.1 (zlib licence).
